{"id":"mahabharata-3-059","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":59,"title":"एकोनषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 59 · Nala abandons Damayanti","summary":{"en":"In a lonely rest-house Damayanti falls asleep sharing her garment with Nala. Driven by Kali and his own despair, Nala cuts the cloth in two with a sword he finds, and after much wavering leaves her sleeping in the empty forest.","kn":"ಏಕಾಂತ ಧರ್ಮಶಾಲೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ದಮಯಂತಿ ತನ್ನ ವಸ್ತ್ರವನ್ನು ನಳನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹಂಚಿಕೊಂಡು ಮಲಗುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಕಲಿಯ ಪ್ರೇರಣೆ ಮತ್ತು ಹತಾಶೆಯಿಂದ ನಳನು ಸಿಕ್ಕ ಕತ್ತಿಯಿಂದ ಬಟ್ಟೆಯನ್ನು ಎರಡಾಗಿ ಕತ್ತರಿಸಿ, ಬಹಳ ಹಿಂಜರಿತದ ನಂತರ ನಿರ್ಜನ ಕಾಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಮಲಗಿದ್ದ ಅವಳನ್ನು ಬಿಟ್ಟು ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"एक सूनी धर्मशाला में दमयन्ती नल के साथ अपना वस्त्र बाँटकर सो जाती हैं। कलि और अपनी निराशा से प्रेरित नल एक मिली तलवार से कपड़े को दो भागों में काटते हैं, और बहुत दुविधा के बाद उन्हें सूने वन में सोती छोड़ जाते हैं।","te":"ఒంటరి సత్రంలో దమయంతి తన వస్త్రాన్ని నలునితో పంచుకొని నిద్రిస్తుంది. కలి ప్రేరణతో, నిరాశతో నలుడు దొరికిన ఖడ్గంతో వస్త్రాన్ని రెండుగా కోసి, ఎంతో సంకోచం తర్వాత నిర్జన అడవిలో నిద్రిస్తున్న ఆమెను విడిచి వెళ్తాడు.","ta":"தனிமையான சத்திரத்தில் தமயந்தி தன் ஆடையை நளனுடன் பகிர்ந்து உறங்குகிறாள். கலியின் தூண்டலாலும் தன் விரக்தியாலும் நளன் கிடைத்த வாளால் துணியை இரண்டாக வெட்டி, நெடுந்தயக்கத்துக்குப் பின் வெறிச்சோடிய காட்டில் உறங்கும் அவளை விட்டுச் செல்கிறான்.","ml":"വഴിയമ്പലത്തിൽ ദമയന്തി നളനോടൊപ്പം വസ്ത്രം പങ്കിട്ടുറങ്ങുന്നു. കലിയുടെ പ്രേരണയാലും സ്വന്തം നിരാശയാലും നളൻ, കിട്ടിയ വാൾകൊണ്ട് വസ്ത്രം രണ്ടായി മുറിക്കുന്നു; ഏറെ സംശയിച്ചശേഷം, ഉറങ്ങുന്ന അവളെ ശൂന്യമായ കാട്ടിൽ ഉപേക്ഷിച്ചുപോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.59; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"इन्द्रलोकाभिगमनपर्व","titleEn":"Indralokabhigamana Parva (Journey to Indra's world)","verses":[{"text":"नल उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Nala said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"यथा राज्यं पितुस्ते तत्तथा मम न संशयः ।\nन तु तत्र गमिष्यामि विषमस्थः कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father's kingdom is mine as much as yours, no doubt. But I will never go there in such misfortune."}},{"n":2,"text":"कथं समृद्धो गत्वाहं तव हर्षविवर्धनः ।\nपरिद्यूनो गमिष्यामि तव शोकविवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I once went there prosperous, adding to your joy; how can I go gambled away, adding to your sorrow?"}},{"text":"बृहदश्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brihadashva said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"इति ब्रुवन्नलो राजा दमयन्तीं पुनः पुनः ।\nसान्त्वयामास कल्याणीं वाससोऽर्धेन संवृताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So King Nala spoke, again and again comforting the good lady, who was covered with half his cloth."}},{"n":4,"text":"तावेकवस्त्रसंवीतावटमानावितस्ततः ।\nक्षुत्पिपासापरिश्रान्तौ सभां कांचिदुपेयतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both wrapped in a single garment, wandering here and there, wearied by hunger and thirst, they came upon a certain shelter."}},{"n":5,"text":"तां सभामुपसंप्राप्य तदा स निषधाधिपः ।\nवैदर्भ्या सहितो राजा निषसाद महीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching that shelter, the lord of the Nishadhas sat down on the ground with the Vidarbha princess."}},{"n":6,"text":"स वै विवस्त्रो मलिनो विकचः पांसुगुण्ठितः ।\nदमयन्त्या सह श्रान्तः सुष्वाप धरणीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Naked, dirty, with matted hair, covered in dust, exhausted, he fell asleep on the bare earth with Damayanti."}},{"n":7,"text":"दमयन्त्यपि कल्याणी निद्रयापहृता ततः ।\nसहसा दुःखमासाद्य सुकुमारी तपस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fair Damayanti too, delicate and ascetic-like in her suffering, was overcome by sleep, having suddenly met such sorrow."}},{"n":8,"text":"सुप्तायां दमयन्त्यां तु नलो राजा विशां पते ।\nशोकोन्मथितचित्तात्मा न स्म शेते यथा पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Damayanti slept, King Nala, lord of people, his mind churned by grief, could not sleep as before."}},{"n":9,"text":"स तद्राज्यापहरणं सुहृत्त्यागं च सर्वशः ।\nवने च तं परिध्वंसं प्रेक्ष्य चिन्तामुपेयिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He thought about the loss of his kingdom, the desertion by his friends, and his ruin in the forest, and fell into worry."}},{"n":10,"text":"किं नु मे स्यादिदं कृत्वा किं नु मे स्यादकुर्वतः ।\nकिं नु मे मरणं श्रेयः परित्यागो जनस्य वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What would come of my doing this, and what if I do not? Would death be better for me, or leaving my people?"}},{"n":11,"text":"मामियं ह्यनुरक्तेदं दुःखमाप्नोति मत्कृते ।\nमद्विहीना त्वियं गच्छेत्कदाचित्स्वजनं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"She loves me and suffers this sorrow for my sake. Without me she might someday go back to her own people."}},{"n":12,"text":"मया निःसंशयं दुःखमियं प्राप्स्यत्यनुत्तमा ।\nउत्सर्गे संशयः स्यात्तु विन्देतापि सुखं क्वचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With me she will surely have sorrow, the best of women. If I leave her, there is doubt, but she may find some happiness.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"स विनिश्चित्य बहुधा विचार्य च पुनः पुनः ।\nउत्सर्गेऽमन्यत श्रेयो दमयन्त्या नराधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After deciding in many ways and pondering again and again, the king concluded that leaving Damayanti was better."}},{"n":14,"text":"सोऽवस्त्रतामात्मनश्च तस्याश्चाप्येकवस्त्रताम् ।\nचिन्तयित्वाध्यगाद्राजा वस्त्रार्धस्यावकर्तनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking of his own nakedness and her having only one garment, the king hit upon cutting the cloth in half."}},{"n":15,"text":"कथं वासो विकर्तेयं न च बुध्येत मे प्रिया ।\nचिन्त्यैवं नैषधो राजा सभां पर्यचरत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How can I cut the cloth so that my beloved does not wake?\" So thinking, the Nishadha king moved about the shelter."}},{"n":16,"text":"परिधावन्नथ नल इतश्चेतश्च भारत ।\nआससाद सभोद्देशे विकोशं खड्गमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Nala ran this way and that, descendant of Bharata, he found a fine, unsheathed sword in a corner of the shelter."}},{"n":17,"text":"तेनार्धं वाससश्छित्त्वा निवस्य च परंतपः ।\nसुप्तामुत्सृज्य वैदर्भीं प्राद्रवद्गतचेतनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With it he cut the cloth in half, dressed himself in his share, and, scorcher of foes, left the sleeping Vidarbha princess and ran off, out of his senses."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततो निबद्धहृदयः पुनरागम्य तां सभाम् ।\nदमयन्तीं तथा दृष्ट्वा रुरोद निषधाधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, his heart bound to her, he came back to the shelter, and seeing Damayanti, the lord of the Nishadhas wept."}},{"n":19,"text":"यां न वायुर्न चादित्यः पुरा पश्यति मे प्रियाम् ।\nसेयमद्य सभामध्ये शेते भूमावनाथवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"She whom neither wind nor sun used to see, my beloved, now lies in the middle of a shelter on the ground like one without protector."}},{"n":20,"text":"इयं वस्त्रावकर्तेन संवीता चारुहासिनी ।\nउन्मत्तेव वरारोहा कथं बुद्ध्वा भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wrapped in a torn cloth, sweet-smiling, fine-hipped, how will she be when she wakes, like one mad?"}},{"n":21,"text":"कथमेका सती भैमी मया विरहिता शुभा ।\nचरिष्यति वने घोरे मृगव्यालनिषेविते ॥","meaning":{"en":"How will good Bhima's daughter, parted from me, go alone through a dreadful forest frequented by beasts and snakes?\""}},{"n":22,"text":"गत्वा गत्वा नलो राजा पुनरेति सभां मुहुः ।\nआकृष्यमाणः कलिना सौहृदेनापकृष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Nala went and returned to the shelter again and again, pulled away by Kali and drawn back by love."}},{"n":23,"text":"द्विधेव हृदयं तस्य दुःखितस्याभवत्तदा ।\nदोलेव मुहुरायाति याति चैव सभां मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His heart was as if split in two; in his sorrow he came and went to the shelter like a swing."}},{"n":24,"text":"सोऽपकृष्टस्तु कलिना मोहितः प्राद्रवन्नलः ।\nसुप्तामुत्सृज्य तां भार्यां विलप्य करुणं बहु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Finally, dragged off by Kali and deluded, Nala ran away, leaving his sleeping wife, lamenting piteously."}},{"n":25,"text":"नष्टात्मा कलिना स्पृष्टस्तत्तद्विगणयन्नृपः ।\nजगामैव वने शून्ये भार्यामुत्सृज्य दुःखितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his mind lost, touched by Kali, the king went into the empty forest, weighing this and that, grieving, leaving his wife behind."}}]}]}